    "class": "gps-633779858002018903 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/photobrickusa/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=633779857901224535&sectionId=633779858002018903)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggvjCkntfh9_text","label":"ggvjCkntfh9_text","default":"More Than Just a Drawing"},{"type":"html","id":"ggbM3amxFUd_text","label":"ggbM3amxFUd_text","default":"<p>Memobrick gives children's artwork a completely different life.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A drawing can be transformed into a personalized brick mosaic, allowing your child to build their own creation piece by piece.</p><p>They can watch as the individual bricks slowly come together and begin to resemble the artwork they originally created.</p><p>The experience can feel almost magical.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Something that started as a drawing on a piece of paper becomes something they can physically build, touch, and display.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg-Ywx9TYLB_text","label":"gg-Ywx9TYLB_text","default":"<p><strong>\"You Drew It. Now Let's Build It.\"</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggkODTUcQ65_text","label":"ggkODTUcQ65_text","default":"<p>Imagine showing your child their favorite drawing and telling them that they are going to build it themselves.</p><p>Instead of simply putting the artwork in a frame, you can turn it into a hands on activity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Parents and children can sit together and work through the pieces. Older children may enjoy building independently, while younger children can participate with help from their family.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The building process can become just as memorable as the finished piece.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggyr_7_x8Ko_text","label":"ggyr_7_x8Ko_text","default":"<p><strong>Make Their Creativity Part of Your Home</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg5Md4eKz6X_text","label":"gg5Md4eKz6X_text","default":"<p>Children's artwork often ends up on refrigerators, bedroom doors, or inside storage boxes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Those little displays can be wonderful, but a personalized Memobrick gives a special creation a more permanent place.</p><p>Display it in their bedroom, playroom, family room, or another space where everyone can see it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It becomes more than home décor. It becomes a reminder of their imagination and the stage of childhood when they created it.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYOMGZS7IM_text","label":"ggYOMGZS7IM_text","default":"<p><strong>What Can You Turn Into a Memobrick?</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggNCcZVnCT-_text","label":"ggNCcZVnCT-_text","default":"<p>You do not have to limit yourself to traditional drawings.</p><p>Consider turning these creations into keepsakes:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A child's favorite drawing</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A picture of the family</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• Their dream house</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A drawing of their favorite animal</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A picture of a superhero</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• Their dream car</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A drawing made for Mom or Dad</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• Artwork created for Grandma or Grandpa</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A school art project</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>• A funny drawing that tells a memorable story</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The more personal the artwork, the more meaningful the finished keepsake can become.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Children's artwork can also make an incredibly personal gift.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Imagine giving a parent a Memobrick created from a drawing their child made specifically for them.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Or imagine a grandparent receiving a mosaic based on a picture created by their grandchild.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It is not simply a personalized gift. It is something that came directly from the child's imagination.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This makes it especially meaningful for birthdays, Mother's Day, Father's Day, Christmas, Grandparents' Day, or simply as a surprise.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggSI7IZ3r9s_text","label":"ggSI7IZ3r9s_text","default":"<p><strong>Build It Together</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg-Iimb0okV_text","label":"gg-Iimb0okV_text","default":"<p>One of the best parts of turning a child's artwork into a Memobrick is that the process can become a family activity.</p><p>Parents can help younger children find and assemble the pieces. Older children can take pride in building their own artwork.</p><p>While building, families can talk about the original drawing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Why did they draw that character?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What does the picture represent?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Why did they choose those colors?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What story were they imagining?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Those conversations can create another memory connected to the artwork.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The amount of detail in the artwork can help determine the Memobrick size.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Simple drawings with one main subject can work well with smaller sizes. If the drawing contains several characters, lots of details, words, or a larger scene, choosing a bigger size can give the artwork more room.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For more detailed artwork, a larger Memobrick can help preserve important elements and make the finished design easier to appreciate.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggFexn6Bi2G_text","label":"ggFexn6Bi2G_text","default":"<p><strong>Watch Their Imagination Grow</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gglU5tLVIWW_text","label":"gglU5tLVIWW_text","default":"<p>One drawing can capture a small moment in a child's development, but a collection of drawings can tell an entire story.</p><p>You could preserve artwork from different ages and create a visual timeline of your child's creativity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Their first simple drawings can eventually be followed by more detailed artwork, showing how their skills and imagination developed over the years.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What starts as a single keepsake could become a collection of memories that your family treasures.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_label","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_label","default":"Add to cart"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_outOfStockLabel","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_outOfStockLabel","default":"Out Of Stock"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_unavailableLabel","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_unavailableLabel","default":"Unavailable"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_variantSelectionRequiredMessage","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_variantSelectionRequiredMessage","default":"Please select a variant to add product to cart"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_successMessage","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_successMessage","default":"Add product to cart successfully"},{"type":"html","id":"ggoN39zkcwt_errorMessage","label":"ggoN39zkcwt_errorMessage","default":"Cannot add product to cart"},{"type":"html","id":"ggcoRiuOidl_text","label":"ggcoRiuOidl_text","default":"<p><i>A child's imagination can create worlds that adults might never think of.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i>A simple drawing can represent a dream, a story, a person they love, or something that exists entirely inside their imagination.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i>Memobrick gives you a way to take that imagination off the page and turn it into something they can build.</i></p><p><i><strong>They imagined it. They drew it. Now they can build it.</strong></i></p>"}],
